 "_note": "Language-neutral structure of the first-boot flow (first_boot_script.py validates it; labs/first-boot drives it). One step per first_boot.ITEMS id plus 'hello' and 'done'. NO words here: what Zoe says and what the panel shows are in first_boot_<lang>.json under the same step id. 'mode' is how the step is done: voice (she asks, the person answers), physical (a guided spoken routine at the panel), pinpad (the panel PIN pad, the one keyboard VISION allows), qr (a QR on the panel, finished on the phone), system (the unit does it itself, no person). 'backed_by.status' is the honest state of the mechanism the step needs TODAY: exists | partial | missing (docs/architecture/first-boot.md ranks the missing ones). 'on' maps every person behaviour to a transition; the validator fails a step that leaves a behaviour unmapped or maps it to something that does not move forward. 'budget_s' is the DECLARED time budget of a step that goes well, not a measurement.",
 "behaviours": ["yes", "done", "later", "no", "silence", "unclear", "fail", "child", "walk_away", "resume"],
